    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0735" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2343: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-05T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 7—7:44
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>My December 3, 5 p.m.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d591-f1"/> Representative of Chita
                    government states that conference which was to be held at Manchouli has been <pb
                        facs="0736" n="612" xml:id="pg612"/> called off and in its place the
                    previous negotiations at Peking regarding commercial relations will be resumed.
                    He says that Far Eastern Republic advises that the question of the Chinese
                    Eastern be allowed to rest until after the discussion at the Washington
                    Conference. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
